[ITERATION 2 / visual review and measured result]
Opened individually: OUT/it2/review/close-000-pair.png, close-035-pair.png, close-090-pair.png, close-180-pair.png, close-below-pair.png. Baseline is next to candidate in each.
What I see: The front now has a continuous pale tuft band, but its hard, regular top edge looks like an attached beard. Long tips hang over the collar. At 35 degrees, the lower-left tufts stretch into broad parallel ribbons; the side view shows an obvious shelf projecting toward the shoulder; the below view exposes large flat cards along the jaw. The rear remains visually unchanged. The nose, mouth, and eyes are not covered. This does not look like a natural ruff.
OUT/review2.log and OUT/it2/review/noise-summary.json record noise.chin at 2.9569829840399273 against a paired baseline of 3.709117400328865; this is an improvement but still FAILS against the 1.3 threshold. Geometry and unchanged-byte evidence: OUT/it2/build.json and invariants.json.
Final allowed iteration change: use more, narrower, and shorter cards; raise the upper layer toward the cheek/mouth underside; stagger roots to break the beard boundary; lower the tint toward the source grey; and prevent drape onto distant collar/chest hits. Smoothing remains the same as iteration 2. Save explicit draped per-card geometry in the layout so the handoff records the actual curved mesh, not just the pre-drape controls. Single author-script change for this iteration. Parameters: OUT/recipe3.json.
Next costly step: final candidate paired Cycles orbit, below, and game-scale renders. This is build/render/look iteration 3 of 3; no additional iterations are authorized.
